Task: write a StableHLO program whose entry function has exactly this signature:
func.func @main(%x: tensor<8xf32>) -> tensor<22xf32>

It must compute: out has length 22: out[3 * i] = x[i] and every other element is 0.0 (2 zero(s) inserted between consecutive elements, none at the ends).

Relevant operations: pad, constant.

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<8xf32>) -> tensor<22xf32> {
  %c0 = stablehlo.constant dense<0.0> : tensor<f32>
  %out = "stablehlo.pad"(%x, %c0) {
    edge_padding_low = array<i64: 0>,
    edge_padding_high = array<i64: 0>,
    interior_padding = array<i64: 2>
  } : (tensor<8xf32>, tensor<f32>) -> tensor<22xf32>
  return %out : tensor<22xf32>
}
```

