Task: write a StableHLO program whose entry function has exactly this signature:
func.func @main(%x: tensor<6x8xf32>, %i: tensor<i32>) -> tensor<2x8xf32>

It must compute: out = rows s .. s+1 of x, where s = min(max(i, 0), 4) (the start row is clamped so the window stays inside x).

Relevant operations: dynamic_slice, constant.

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<6x8xf32>, %i: tensor<i32>) -> tensor<2x8xf32> {
  %c0 = stablehlo.constant dense<0> : tensor<i32>
  %c4 = stablehlo.constant dense<4> : tensor<i32>
  %c1 = stablehlo.constant dense<1> : tensor<i32>

  // Clamp i to be at least 0: max(i, 0)
  %max_i_0 = "stablehlo.maximum"(%i, %c0) : (tensor<i32>, tensor<i32>) -> tensor<i32>
  // Clamp max_i_0 to be at most 4: min(max(i,0), 4)
  %s = "stablehlo.minimum"(%max_i_0, %c4) : (tensor<i32>, tensor<i32>) -> tensor<i32>

  // dynamic_slice expects start indices as scalars (tensor<i32>), but stablehlo.dynamic_slice takes tensor<I> for each start index.
  // The input is 2D: shape 6x8, so we need 2 start indices: s for rows, 0 for columns.
  %c0_col = stablehlo.constant dense<0> : tensor<i32>

  %out = "stablehlo.dynamic_slice"(%x, %s, %c0_col) {slice_sizes = array<i64: 2, 8>} : (tensor<6x8xf32>, tensor<i32>, tensor<i32>) -> tensor<2x8xf32>
  return %out : tensor<2x8xf32>
}
```

