Task: write a StableHLO program whose entry function has exactly this signature:
func.func @main(%x: tensor<4x3x5xf32>, %v: tensor<3xf32>) -> tensor<4x3x5xf32>

It must compute: out[a, n, b] = x[a, n, b] - v[n] for all a, n, b.

Relevant operations: broadcast_in_dim, element-wise ops (add/subtract/multiply/divide/maximum/minimum/negate/exponential/sqrt/rsqrt/abs).

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<2x6xf32>, %y: tensor<2x4xf32>) -> tensor<2x10xf32> {
  %r = "stablehlo.concatenate"(%x, %y) {dimension = 1 : i64} : (tensor<2x6xf32>, tensor<2x4xf32>) -> tensor<2x10xf32>
  return %r : tensor<2x10xf32>
}
```

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<6x6xf32>) -> tensor<6x6xf32> {
  %c6 = constant 6 : index
  %c0 = constant 0 : index
  %c0f = constant 0.0 : f32

  // Create iota for rows: shape [6,6], iota along dim 0
  %iota_rows = stablehlo.iota %c6 : tensor<6x6xf32>, dim = 0

  // Create iota for cols: shape [6,6], iota along dim 1
  %iota_cols = stablehlo.iota %c6 : tensor<6x6xf32>, dim = 1

  // Compare j <= i: iota_cols <= iota_rows
  %cmp = stablehlo.compare %iota_cols, %iota_rows {
    comparison_direction = "le"
  } : tensor<6x6xf32>

  // Select: if cmp true, take x[i,j], else 0.0
  %out = stablehlo.select %cmp, %x, %c0f : tensor<6x6xf32>

  func.return %out : tensor<6x6xf32>
}
```

