Task: write a StableHLO program whose entry function has exactly this signature:
func.func @main(%x: tensor<7x3xf32>) -> tensor<7xf32>

It must compute: out = the arithmetic mean of x over dimension 1 (that dimension is removed).

Relevant operations: reduce, constant, element-wise ops (add/subtract/multiply/divide/maximum/minimum/negate/exponential/sqrt/rsqrt/abs).

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
func.func @main(%x: tensor<7x3xf32>) -> tensor<7xf32> {
  %c0 = stablehlo.constant dense<0.0> : tensor<f32>
  %init = stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim %c0 : tensor<f32> to tensor<7x3xf32> {broadcast_dimensions = dense<0, 1> : tensor<2xi64>}
  %sum = "stablehlo.reduce"(%x, %init) ({
    ^bb0(%a: tensor<f32>, %b: tensor<f32>):
      %add = stablehlo.add %a, %b : tensor<f32>
      stablehlo.return %add : tensor<f32>
  }) {dimensions = dense<1> : tensor<1xi64>} : (tensor<7x3xf32>, tensor<7x3xf32>) -> tensor<7xf32>
  %c3 = stablehlo.constant dense<3.0> : tensor<f32>
  %c3_broadcast = stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim %c3 : tensor<f32> to tensor<7xf32> {broadcast_dimensions = dense<0> : tensor<1xi64>}
  %mean = stablehlo.divide %sum, %c3_broadcast : tensor<7xf32>
  return %mean : tensor<7xf32>
}
```

